course: dictionary
lesson: 12031
title: Choral
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Choral» is an adjective, a describing word. It tells you that something is to do with a choir, which is a group of people who sing together. Choral music is music sung by a choir.
explain: Context clues help you here. «The whole school sang in the choral concert.» A concert where the whole school sings is a concert of many voices together, so choral must be about singing as a group.
explain: Choral also works in class. «Our class did a choral reading of a poem about the sea.» Everyone read the poem out loud at the same time. Check it: swap in the words together and out loud, and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Choral means to do with a choir, or sung by a choir.
fact: Choral also means said or spoken by a group together, as in a choral reading.
fact: Choral music, choral society, choral speaking and choral reading are phrases you may meet.
fact: A choir is a group of people who sing together.
fact: Choral sounds the same as coral, but it is about voices, not the reef in the sea.
exercise: «The whole school sang in the choral concert.» What does choral mean here? | A quiet, lonely song | A race run by one runner | *To do with a choir, sung by many voices together | A kind of painting
exercise: «Our class did a choral reading of a poem about the sea.» What does a choral reading mean? | One child reads alone while the rest listen | The poem is written on the board | The poem is read in a whisper | *The whole class reads the poem out loud together
exercise: Mum says, «I sing in the choral society.» Which is the best meaning of choral? | Something to do with the sea | *Part of a choir, singing with a group | Happening in a library | Very loud and bossy
test: «Choral music is music sung by a choir.» Choral music is music that is what? | Silent, with no voices | Read from a book | *Sung by a choir | Played on one piano
test: Which phrase means a group saying a poem together? | *Choral reading | Choral ride | Choral drawing | Choral painting
exam: Lily joined the choral society, so she is in a group that does what? | Paints pictures alone | *Sings together with other voices | Reads in silence in the library | Runs races on the field
